+# Authenticated activation and export candidate
+
+The deployed 9d36318ddc03 image allows anonymous book creation and exports, and accepts owner changes through the project serializer. The candidate requires authentication for the library and export endpoints, makes owner read-only, preserves scoped 404s, and explicitly retires the unimplemented legacy export queue. The browser export modal now calls the existing authFetch helper so token and JWT sessions send credentials.
+
+31 isolated PostgreSQL/MinIO checks passed, including signup, save/return, cross-account denial, owner immutability, two-page PDF output, signed PDF/preview downloads and unsigned-object denial. The test creates only synthetic accounts. Run scripts/qa/activation_permissions_check.py only in a disposable isolated PostgreSQL/MinIO environment; its database guard requires memoire-qa-pg/activationqa. Production is not modified by that test.
+
+This is a staging candidate. Browser acceptance, paid entitlements/limits, malformed export payload/size limits, public showcase authorization and comprehensive privacy/security review remain open. Do not advertise printing, paid export entitlements or full launch readiness from this evidence alone.
